e number in the timing table is wrong, and one of the map's main findings rests on it.\n\n**The error.** The p50 for the \"Editor.bin received\" mark is not 3,339 ms. The five runs were 3390, 2973, 3339, 1996 and 3220 ms. Sorted, that is 1996, 2973, 3220, 3339, 3390, so the median is **3,220 ms**. I checked every other mark the same way, and they are all correct.\n\n**What that changes.**\n- The `editor-bin-download` stage should be 3,220 − 2,878 = **342 ms (6.9 %)**, not 461 ms (9.3 %).\n- The window from receiving Editor.bin to load complete becomes 4,503 − 3,220 = **1,283 ms**, not 1,164 ms. So the estimated split across sdkjs-word, sdkjs-common, web-apps and browser needs to be recomputed.\n- The total still adds up to 4,974 ms, but the per-module figures and shares change, for both project and the client-side modules.\n- The comparison section says the Editor.bin download share is \"9.3 % vs 4.3 %\", about double the 10-page sample. With the correct number it is 6.9 % vs 4.3 %. The executor's report and log repeat the \"doubling\" claim, and it would go into the Atlas as a lesson unless it is fixed.\n\n**What is otherwise sound.**\n- The runner is a faithful copy of the 10-page runner.\n- The yaml stages add up to the total, and every stage above 5 % names its functions.\n- The executor log is filled in.\n- The caveats are stated honestly: the client split is an estimate based on the PKT-0043 profile, and x2t still loads the packaged `sdk-all.bin`.\n\n**Smaller items to fix while revising:**\n- The map lists a follow-up (profile the client window for this sample) that is neither in `.theseus/spawn/` nor under \"Spawned packets\". It should be filed with `theseus packet new`.\n- The packet's \"Lessons for the Atlas\" section is empty, although the executor's report lists two lessons.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT Editor.bin-received p50 is 3220 ms not 3339; recompute editor-bin-download (342 ms, 6.9 %), the 1283 ms client split, module totals and the comparison claim; also